WEBVTT

NOTE The narration of See the investment inside the house, generated by tools/captions.mjs from the voiceover's timing.

1
00:00:01.750 --> 00:00:04.120
You run a few houses by the room,

2
00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:05.620
and you run them well.

3
00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:07.670
Now you've spotted the next one,

4
00:00:07.670 --> 00:00:10.450
a six-bedroom house near the greenway.

5
00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:13.640
So you work it out the way everyone does:

6
00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:17.490
rooms, times weekly rent, times occupancy.

7
00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:19.140
That's the right formula.

8
00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:21.380
But you picked the rent yourself,

9
00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:23.930
and the ninety percent is a guess.

10
00:00:23.930 --> 00:00:25.660
And nobody has counted

11
00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:29.170
the other houses renting rooms nearby.

12
00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:31.800
You make the offer on those numbers,

13
00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:33.870
and the house is yours.

14
00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:36.420
Then the rooms go up for rent,

15
00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:39.670
and two of them sit empty for weeks.

16
00:00:40.070 --> 00:00:43.400
Seventeen other houses within three miles

17
00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:45.840
were renting rooms all along.

18
00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:49.510
If your rooms fill seventy-five percent

19
00:00:49.510 --> 00:00:52.390
of the time instead of ninety percent,

20
00:00:52.390 --> 00:00:54.950
that's seven hundred eighty-three dollars

21
00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:57.090
a month off your plan.

22
00:00:57.190 --> 00:01:00.600
The formula was fine all along.

23
00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:04.680
The numbers inside it just had nothing behind them.

24
00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:09.510
RoomIQ puts evidence behind each of those numbers,

25
00:01:09.510 --> 00:01:11.470
before you make the offer.

26
00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:14.280
Type in the address, and it counts and maps

27
00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:17.850
the co-living houses within about three miles.

28
00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:20.220
Add each room and its bath,

29
00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:22.140
and the rent and occupancy come

30
00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:24.550
from comparable rooms nearby.

31
00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:27.320
Then it prints the estimate with its formula,

32
00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:30.860
its comps, and a label for how sure it is.

33
00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:32.430
And when the evidence is thin,

34
00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:33.740
it says so.

35
00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:38.050
So you're back at the same table with the same formula,

36
00:01:38.050 --> 00:01:41.230
and every number has its evidence beside it.

37
00:01:41.230 --> 00:01:43.520
You read the label before the number,

38
00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:46.490
and you test the deal with your own costs.

39
00:01:46.490 --> 00:01:48.060
Then you make the offer,

40
00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:50.370
knowing what each number rests on.

41
00:01:50.970 --> 00:01:55.330
RoomIQ. See the investment inside the house.
